      "172": {
        "attributes": {
          "alignment": {
            "type": "integer",
            "value": 0
          },
          "fill": {
            "type": "bool",
            "value": true
          },
          "font-size": {
            "type": "float",
            "value": 19
          },
          "text": {
            "type": "string",
            "value": "Distortion\n\nThis patch demonstrates how to create many kinds of distortion effects.\n\nIn this example we create a texture by using collections of random float values, but you could do the same with shapes, fractal noise, static, metaballs, video content or a picture of your cat.\nThe core concept is to create a “source” texture to distort the incoming texture using the UV-Offset node.\n\nTo get the most out of this example we recommend that you check out the basic tutorials and the instancing tutorials. The easiest way to get started is to navigate to the dashboard panel, select either Wire Logo or Test Card as the Texture In source and play around with the parameters.\n"
          }
        },
        "bounds": {
          "height": 241.11404418945312,
          "width": 755.6961669921875,
          "x": -3623.80126953125,
          "y": -584.7699584960938
        },
        "class": {
